title Fold AE -- the escort, its wire reader, and the owner that came home
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The REDS ledger stands at 110 rows and its newest, REDS %110, reads CLOSED at 20260821.073606. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is free.
think Council rota, lap index 593 kyri logs mod 27 -> item 26, active-designing/20260812-171050_the-1024-round-itinerary.md. Deep-read. It names the filling law this loop runs under -- Lindy-first crux-first orders everything, reds preempt across any boundary, a quest is filled rather than invented, and the custody gates are the fence. It also names the atomic unit plainly: one keystone, witnessed, sent as its own signed increment. A fold is exactly that unit.
think The running thread came off the newest log's recommend line: the printed queue named escort_the_word at 31 rungs by 47 lines, 1,410 carried, with start_one at 40 by 35 behind it -- and the standing instruction to hash the family before trusting the count, then read the reach closure for whole families rather than merely for words to widen.
think Hashed every escort_the_word on the ladder. Thirty-two bodies at forty-seven lines: thirty-one byte for byte alike, and abide.rye apart by four lines, every one of the four the same shape -- the owner reaches its own report directly where every rung above reaches through abiding_of. Fourth tier owner in five laps to wear that signature.
think This one came home rather than staying home, and the difference is the whole reading. An owner stays home when a shape born after it dates it out, as hear.rye was dated in fold U -- no accessor gives a body back a check it never had. An owner comes home when the only thing between its body and its cohort's is a reach it never needed to name. abide.rye had no abiding_of at all, so three lines of identity accessor made its forty-seven byte for byte the cohort's, exactly as relent.rye did in fold X and repose.rye in fold Y. The family folded whole at thirty-two.
think Fold Z's rule ran next. escort_the_word reaches fourteen symbols beyond the accessor and all fourteen already stood public in all thirty-one rungs, so the fold's whole price was the twenty-three rungs where abiding_of stood private, plus the three lines the owner gained.
think Reading one hop out found one of the fourteen standing as a whole carrying family above the harness line: dispute_recorded, a wire reader in thirty-three rungs at fourteen lines apiece, one text with no absentee at all. Its five reached symbols were already public in all thirty-three and Dir is the harness's own alias for std.Io.Dir, so it lifted for no widening whatsoever. The other reached bodies -- published_unattended, escorted_in, alone_in, unrecorded_escort, quotes, abide_note at three lines, abide_refusal at seven -- stay home, and several of them are split families a widening would have to heal first.
obs The fold script glob caught caravan/ladder_checks.rye itself and delegated the two harness bodies it had just written back to the harness. Caught by reading the harness tail before building rather than by a failing compile, and repaired by rebuilding both bodies from the pre-fold git text. The lesson is that a harness living in the same directory as its rungs is inside every glob that names them; the next fold script excludes it by name.
obs The arithmetic closes with no remainder. Out went 30x47 and 32x14 at 1,858; back came thirty-two and thirty-three rungs at three lines apiece, carrying 31x3 and 32x3, or 189. The fall of 1,669 stood against a meter reading 1,669. Carrying families held at 707 because both families folded whole, with no visibility split opened and none healed.
obs The lesson this lap adds is that a tier owner is a question rather than a verdict. Five owners have now stood apart from their cohorts and the arc has answered each differently on evidence: hear.rye stayed home on a meaning, amend.rye and appeal.rye and refer.rye stayed home for want of an accessor, abide.rye came home because the accessor cost three lines and folded forty-seven. The test is never who owns the tier -- it is whether the differing lines carry a meaning or merely a reach, and only reading them can say which.
